# ANATOMY — FILE TREE (create exactly this)

```
jonatech-docs-agent/
├── .cursorrules            ← this work order (state, not history — mark CONSUMED when done)
├── README.md               ← one screen: what it is, how to run, demo script
├── requirements.txt        ← fastmcp, openai, mcp, fastapi, uvicorn, jinja2, python-dotenv
├── config.toml             ← model name + provider toggle (xai | openrouter)
├── .env.example           ← XAI_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY (never commit real keys)
├── agent.py                ← the loop: chat → Grok (function calling) → tool dispatch → reply
├── ui.py                   ← 1-file FastAPI web chat (projector-friendly). Fallback: terminal chat in agent.py
├── mcp_client.py           ← stdio MCP client for Paper's server (spawn `paper mcp`)
├── vault_server.py         ← OUR FastMCP server: brain + knowledge + skills + vault
├── brand/jonatech-digital/
│   ├── style.md            ← document-family rules: colors, type scale, spacing, footer, voice
│   ├── assets/             ← REAL Jonatech Digital logo(s) Jonatech drops in + favicon
│   └── templates/proposal.html   ← Jinja2 skeleton: the ONE template
├── knowledge/              ← numbered company files, loaded IN ORDER at wake-up
│   ├── 1_Brand_DNA.md      ← who Jonatech Digital is, positioning, tone
│   ├── 2_Clients.md        ← client list + per-client quirks (rates, terms, preferences)
│   ├── 3_Services_and_Pricing.md ← service catalog + standard rates
│   └── SOUL.md             ← agent persona: how it speaks, how it refuses, its name
├── brain/CONTEXT.md        ← STATUS (rewritten in place) + DECISIONS (appended, dated)
├── .agents/skills/
│   ├── proposal.md         ← procedure + dated LESSONS section (grows itself)
│   └── skills-lock.json    ← versioned skill registry
└── docs/
    ├── EXECUTION_LOG.md    ← dated decisions, one line each
    └── demo/               ← demo script + screenshots
```

---

# THE VAULT SERVER (vault_server.py) — TOOL CONTRACT (FastMCP, stdio)

Implement EXACTLY these tools. Grok's function-calling surface = these + Paper's tools (discovered live).

```
load_brain() -> str
    # Returns brain/CONTEXT.md verbatim. If the file is missing/corrupt,
    # return "⚠️ BRAIN NOT LOADED" — the agent must REFUSE to render in that state.
rewrite_status(section: str, new_text: str) -> str
    # STATUS lines are rewritten IN PLACE, one true answer per fact. Never appended.
append_decision(text: str) -> str
    # Prepends "- YYYY-MM-DD: <text>" under "## DECISIONS". Immutable once written.
load_knowledge() -> str
    # Concatenates knowledge/ files in numeric order (1_, 2_, 3_, SOUL.md last).
read_skill(doc_type: str) -> str   # doc_type="proposal" only in v0.1
    # Returns .agents/skills/proposal.md, procedure + LESSONS.
append_lesson(doc_type: str, lesson: str) -> str
    # Appends "- [YYYY-MM-DD] <lesson>" under "## LESSONS" in the skill file.
    # Bumps skills-lock.json version. Procedure knowledge ONLY — facts go to DECISIONS.
read_brand_style(brand: str) -> str   # brand="jonatech-digital"
    # Returns brand/jonatech-digital/style.md.
read_template(doc_type: str) -> str
    # Returns templates/proposal.html source. The ONLY render source. No freehand HTML.
```

All paths resolve relative to the project root. Validate every input (doc_type/brand must match allow-lists — proposal only, jonatech-digital only) and return clean errors, never exceptions.

---

# AGENT PROTOCOL (agent.py) — THE FOUR-CALL WAKE-UP

System prompt for Grok (write it into agent.py as a constant):

```
You are Jonatech Docs Agent — a document team member for Jonatech Digital.
Before ANY render you MUST, in order: (1) load_brain, (2) load_knowledge,
(3) read_skill("proposal"), (4) read_brand_style("jonatech-digital").
If load_brain returns "⚠️ BRAIN NOT LOADED" — announce it and REFUSE to render.
You never invent brand: template comes from read_template, content comes from
the user request + knowledge. Render onto the Paper drafts file, one page per
proposal, then get_screenshot and self-check before replying.
```

**Render pipeline:** request → wake-up (4 loads) → `read_template("proposal")` → Grok fills Jinja2 placeholders using knowledge (client, service, rate) + request → write HTML layers to Paper via Paper MCP → `get_screenshot` → verify (logo present, colors match style.md, footer has TIN/contact) → reply with summary.

**Fix loop (P2):** user says "fix my comments" → list comments on the page (Paper MCP) → for EACH: edit the layer(s) → `get_screenshot` verify → resolve the comment → report fixed items. **If a comment encodes a durable preference** (e.g. "always put the price last") → `append_decision` AND `append_lesson("proposal", ...)` BEFORE resolving. **Fact → DECISIONS, procedure → LESSONS.**

**Model routing (config.toml):** default `grok-4-fast` via `https://api.x.ai/v1` (OpenAI-compatible, XAI_API_KEY — already in Jonatech's X Subscription shared pool). Fallback: any OpenRouter model via OPENROUTER_API_KEY. One config flip, zero code change.

---

# PAPER INTEGRATION (mcp_client.py)

- Paper Desktop must be RUNNING with the demo file open. Paper's MCP server: spawn `paper mcp` (stdio; the CLI installs at ~/.paper/bin/paper) — legacy HTTP endpoint 127.0.0.1:29979/mcp only works while a file is open. **There is NO hosted/remote Paper MCP — do not attempt tunneling.**
- At build start: run `tools/list` on Paper's server and print the discovered surface. Read `get_guide(topic="paper-mcp-instructions")` ONCE per session (the docs prescribe this — follow it).
- New proposals go on their own page in the drafts file. Exports land in Downloads/ — copy the paths from the tool response.
- Free-plan MCP call limits are REAL. Rehearse early; if limits bite, upgrade to Paper Pro immediately (cheap insurance, Jonatech approves).

